---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, pathFor } from '../../config/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="Legal and privacy information" description="Official Golden Moments legal pages: mobile app privacy policy, website privacy, terms, safety information, privacy choices, and support.">
  <section class="interior-hero">
    <div class="reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Golden Moments / Information</p>
      <h1>Legal and privacy information</h1>
      <p class="interior-lede">A clear place to find the information that matters before you download, play, or share a picture.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="reading-column prose-page">
    <h2><a href={pathFor('/app-privacy/')}>Mobile app privacy policy</a></h2>
    <p>How the app handles local pictures, preferences, support requests, backups, third-party services, and your choices.</p>
    <h2><a href={pathFor('/privacy-choices/')}>Privacy choices and deletion</a></h2>
    <p>Practical instructions for deleting app-owned copies without deleting original photos, managing backups, and requesting deletion of support correspondence.</p>
    <h2><a href={pathFor('/terms/')}>Terms and app license</a></h2>
    <p>Website terms and a direct reference to Apple's standard licensed-application agreement.</p>
    <h2><a href={pathFor('/safety/')}>Safety and medical-use information</a></h2>
    <p>Why Golden Moments is for recreation, not diagnosis, cognitive testing, treatment, or urgent care.</p>
    <h2><a href={pathFor('/privacy/')}>Website privacy notice</a></h2>
    <p>How this static website works without photo uploads, visitor accounts, or advertising scripts, and what GitHub Pages hosting involves.</p>
    <h2><a href={pathFor('/support/')}>Support and contact</a></h2>
    <p>Contact the developer at <a href={'mailto:' + SUPPORT_EMAIL}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. You can report a problem without sending private photos or medical details.</p>
    <p>Golden Moments is published by <strong>Cloudjet Solutions Pte. Ltd.</strong> in Singapore. Features under development should not be assumed to exist in the currently published App Store version.</p>
    <p class="back-home"><a class="text-link" href={pathFor('/')}>← Back to Golden Moments</a></p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
